      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SANFORD BART (3) gets the first look after missing by only a metre and a half at Wagin as favourite, and his Narrogin 2242m record gives him the right grounding despite the rise from NR up to 39 to NR up to 44. GOODONYA MATE had him covered here two starts back, so the top pick is not without a challenge, but his consistency at the track keeps him on top. GALEOCERDO CUVIER (5) has put two placings together at Collie, draws the front row after a second-row start and brings proven track-and-distance form, with Lachlan Kennelly an added strength. TAYLORS BOY FRED (6) was disappointing as favourite last start, yet he beat SANFORD BART by 0.4m at Narrogin two runs ago and has a strong record with Lauren Harper. GOODONYA MATE (9) drops from NR up to 50 after a solid second here behind My Ultimate Kevvie and looks a danger if he repeats that run.",
